	<div class=3D"cms_plugin textplugin_holder"><h3>GOOD NEWS FOR FREE AND IND=
EPENDENT LOCAL RADIO STATIONS IN SWITZERLAND</h3><p>From now on, there=E2=
=80=99s nothing in the way of broadcasting your programme via DAB digital r=
adio. Digris AG who is managing, among others, Open Broadcast, is to obtain=
 the required broadcast concession from the Federal Office of Communication=
s (OFKOM). Digris AG and Opendigitalradio have worked out the concept for l=
ocal digital radio broadcast in close collaboration with the radio associat=
ions Unikom and Asrok/Svokr.</p><p>Up until now, cost considerations have p=
revented smaller event organisers from broadcast digitally as well. For its=
 DAB distribution,&nbsp;<span class=3D"plugin_link"><a href=3D"https://web.=
archive.org/web/20141222002427/http://www.digris.ch/">Digris AG</a></span>
&nbsp;is using a new, software-supported technology at significantly lower =
cost and which is particularly well suited to smaller coverage areas. The s=
oftware solution was developed by Opendigitalradio. In a first step, the fi=
rst antennas are to be erected in Geneva and Zurich. Overall completion in =
Switzerland is expected to be reached by the end of 2015.</p><p>If you are =
looking for the Openbroadcast radio website please visit&nbsp;<span class=
=3D"plugin_link"><a href=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20141222002427/http=
://www.openbroadcast.ch/">http://www.openbroadcast.ch/</a></span>
</p><h3>Where to go from here?</h3></div><div class=3D"cms_plugin shortcutp=
lugin_holder">

